{16 = 16-19}
16.	But like a tree planted in riverine thickets, I am bowed down in dirt. 
17.	They have bound a rope around my hands, on my chair where they have tied me. 
18.	In my city, where I would wear clean clothes, I am clothed instead in mourning dress. 
19.	When I wash away clods of soil, dust still gets into my eyes. 

{20 = 20-23}
20.	Dogs devour corpses, lifting their chests. 
21.	When dragons kill, what is left from their mouths is put aside. 
22.	Fire consumes reedbeds even though they have waterways. 
23.	@wDN{Utu}, who eats butter, who eats cream, nevertheless touches the table of the poor. 
@vart[t3121.v15,t3121.v15]{@varn{1 ms. adds:} Grant me my life and hold my hands! I am a son of a widow, and I have no one to take care of me. } 

{24 = 24}
24.	As for me, when will the heart of @wRN{Šulgi}, my lord, be restored to me? @vart[t3121.v16,t3121.v16]{@varn{1 ms. adds:} May my lord attend to me and restore me to my mother. } 
